# host/audio: stage short AudioOut tails for large callbacks (PR #2989)
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/2e86b714a3c161a883803058d000abc77bcd8b98  (PR #2989)
# Author:    seedds, 2026-11-21 01:31:29 +0800
# Co-authors:
#   Co-authored-by: gamentk
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); the attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# WHAT IT CHANGES FOR THE PHONE
#   On an iPhone with a Bluetooth output RemoteIO asks for far more than 5 ms per callback. A guest AudioOut that keeps only two buffers in flight could not refill in time: the host held
#   the last, partly played block until drained, so the game was told "released" late and the next callback ran dry (upstream replay: 666 underruns over 8,000 callbacks -> 0, sample exact).
#   Now, for guest AudioOut outputs only (allow_early_release), when a request ends inside a block the remaining tail (at most 10 ms, 480 frames, up to eight channels) is copied into the
#   output's own `staged` buffer and the descriptor is released at once. GetAudioOutBufferCount keeps counting the staged block until consumed (q_played). Stop / restart discard it.
#   OutputStream, the audren sink and the host PCM output are untouched. Default: on, no switch.
#
# HAND-MERGED: five hunks (NX2Apple 0046 / 0048 split the open in au_open_impl / au_open_at and put GetAudioOutBufferCount under g_aos_lock): upstream's 'source' enum replaces au_open_impl's
#   last parameter sink_pcm; its three callers pass it (pcmout_open maps sink_pcm to AU_DEVICE_SINK / AU_PCM_OUT). NOT included: upstream e30aca5e (route-change recovery), LATER.
# RISK: medium (release order of the guest's audio buffers). NOT run on a device. Shader chain id untouched.
#
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0415 and the candidates numbered below this one, in the order of the numbers of this folder.

